R-PX2 R-PX6 R-CC9 R-SO22 R-PH7 R-SO10 R-SO2 R-SO20 R-CV1 R-BL1 R-BL3 R-BL6 R-LD4 R-LD6 R-DL5 R-EC13 (slice 023c, question Q1 for the variable TALON_IN_PROXY): the probes of `update json` (Ladder.run!, with a copy) run the selected compiler by its path. Installed in `toolchains/`: A1 (nightly-2026-10-09-258ab27) and nightly-2026-October-13-91fa0c2 (the other tag form of the pin of p4). The `roc` on PATH is `compiler=<id>`: its file is `$HOME/bin/roc` (the harness). Each run is one project and the held compiler is shown by the program of its probe lines.
The calls of a run that probes: `list_dirs` of `toolchains` (step 0a), `canonical` of the cache dirs (step 0c, it is inside the lines `canonical` of the log: 2 paths), then `random`, `copy_tree` ..., and before each round of probes (2 rounds: the checks, then the build) `write_atomic` of `.last-use` when the compiler is installed (R-CC9). Each probe line has the program and one line `env` with the 3 variables of R-PX6 and R-EV17.
Run 1 (p1): the pin is A1, installed, and PATH has another id: the probes run `toolchains/A1/roc`, `.last-use` is written twice. Run 2 (p2): the pin is the id of PATH and it is not installed: the program is the file of PATH (never the name `roc`), no `.last-use`. Run 3 (p3): the pin is not installed and not on PATH: exit 13, the text of `Compiler.require` (`Run: tln roc install <id>.`), after `list_dirs` and before the copy: no `random`, no probe, no write.
Run 4 (p4): the pin `nightly-2026-10-13-91fa0c2` and the installed dir `nightly-2026-October-13-91fa0c2` are one nightly (R-CV1): the program and the `.last-use` are in the installed dir, and the probe line shows the id of the pin. Run 5 (p5): the pin is A1, A1 is installed, and the `roc` on PATH has the same id (D7 of slice 023): the installed copy runs, not `$HOME/bin/roc`.
Run 6 (p6, `no-check`): the pin is not installed, and no probe runs (R-SO22, R-BL6): no `list_dirs` of `toolchains`, exit 0. Run 7 (p7): no pin, `ROC_TOOLCHAIN` (rank 2) is A1: the probes run A1. Run 8 (p8): no pin, `ROC_TOOLCHAIN` is not installed: exit 13 after `list_dirs`. Run 9 (p9, R-SO20): the pin is the id of PATH and `ROC_TOOLCHAIN` is A1 (installed): the command holds the pin, so the probes run the file of PATH and not A1; A1 gets no `.last-use`.
